From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] venus: VK_EXT_device_generated_commands

vkd3d-proton takes it for ExecuteIndirect tier 1.1 (incrementing constants) and for every ExecuteIndirect that
changes state per command (root constants, vertex/index buffers, root descriptors): without it those record
nothing. The protocol headers are venus-protocol's generator output (git-70991d4c plus the video branch) with
VK_KHR_maintenance8 and VK_EXT_device_generated_commands in its extension list (commands 1100-1108; the token data of
dispatch and draw tokens selects no union member: the tag alone goes on the wire); maintenance8's generated code is
0006's, plus its VkMemoryBarrierAccessFlags3KHR in subpass dependencies. vn_generated_commands.c: indirect commands
layouts and the memory requirements query, passed through; no indirect execution sets (the physical device reports
no stage bindable through them). Preprocessing in one command buffer with another's state (as vkd3d-proton does)
sends that command buffer's batched commands first and the preprocessing right after: the host reads the state when
it records the preprocessing (the GPU hung on a stale pipeline otherwise, Xid 109).
---
